    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are the lead due diligence analyst assessing {{$json.company_name}}.\n\nThree specialist researchers have independently investigated the company.\n\nNEWS RESEARCH\n{{$json.news_research}}\n\nFINANCIAL RESEARCH\n{{$json.financial_research}}\n\nLEADERSHIP RESEARCH\n{{$json.leadership_research}}\n\nYour job is NOT to repeat their research.\n\nSynthesize the evidence across all three research streams and identify what it collectively tells us about the company.\n\nProduce:\n\n1. EXECUTIVE ASSESSMENT\nGive a concise overall assessment of the company's current position.\n\n2. KEY POSITIVE SIGNALS\nIdentify the 3 strongest positive signals supported by the research.\n\n3. KEY RISKS / RED FLAGS\nIdentify the 3 most important risks or concerns.\n\n4. CROSS-SOURCE INSIGHTS\nIdentify connections between news, financial performance and leadership that may not be obvious when each research stream is viewed independently.\n\n5. CONTRADICTIONS OR INFORMATION GAPS\nFlag conflicting evidence, weak evidence, outdated information or important unanswered questions.\n\n6. DUE DILIGENCE QUESTIONS\nGive 5 questions that a senior decision-maker should investigate next.\n\n7. FINAL VERDICT\nRate the company:\nLOW RISK / MODERATE RISK / HIGH RISK\n\nThen explain the rating in no more than 3 sentences.\n\nImportant:\n- Base conclusions only on the supplied research.\n- Do not invent facts.\n- Distinguish facts from inference.\n- If evidence is insufficient, explicitly say so.",
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 3.1,
      "position": [
        1264,
        16
      ],
      "id": "public-due-diligence-analyst",
      "name": "Due Diligence Analyst"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "return [\n  {\n    json: {\n      company_name: $(\"Edit Fields\").first().json.company_name,\n      news_research: $(\"News Researcher\").first().json.output,\n      financial_research: $(\"Financial Researcher\").first().json.output,\n      leadership_research: $(\"Leadership Researcher\").first().json.output\n    }\n  }\n];"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1040,
        16
      ],
      "id": "public-prepare-research",
      "name": "Prepare Research"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "model": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "gpt-5-mini"
        },
        "builtInTools": {},
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatOpenAi",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "position": [
