    {
      "parameters": {
        "schemaType": "manual",
        "inputSchema": "{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"overall_risk\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\"LOW\", \"MODERATE\", \"HIGH\", \"CRITICAL\"]\n    },\n    \"confidence\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\"LOW\", \"MEDIUM\", \"HIGH\"]\n    },\n    \"final_executive_assessment\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"confirmed_findings\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"unresolved_findings\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"contradicted_claims\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"key_risks\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"recommended_actions\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"human_review_required\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\"YES\", \"NO\"]\n    },\n    \"human_review_reason\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"overall_risk\",\n    \"confidence\",\n    \"final_executive_assessment\",\n    \"confirmed_findings\",\n    \"unresolved_findings\",\n    \"contradicted_claims\",\n    \"key_risks\",\n    \"recommended_actions\",\n    \"human_review_required\",\n    \"human_review_reason\"\n  ]\n}"
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.outputParserStructured",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "position": [
        2944,
        432
      ],
      "id": "public-structured-output-parser",
      "name": "Structured Output Parser"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are the Final Adjudicator in a multi-agent corporate due-diligence system.\n\nYour role is NOT to perform new research.\nYour role is to adjudicate between the original analysis, the independent critic, and the subsequent verification results.\n\nCOMPANY:\n{{ $(\"Prepare Research\").first().json.company_name }}\n\n====================\nORIGINAL ANALYST REPORT\n====================\n\n{{ $(\"Due Diligence Analyst\").first().json.output }}\n====================\nINDEPENDENT CRITIC REVIEW\n====================\n\n{{ $(\"Due Diligence Critic\").first().json.output }}\n\n====================\nINDEPENDENT VERIFICATION RESULTS\n====================\n\n{{ JSON.stringify($json.verification_results, null, 2)\n}}\n\nYou must now produce the final executive due-diligence assessment.\n\nADJUDICATION RULES:\n\n1. VERIFIED evidence outranks unsupported claims from either the Analyst or Critic.\n\n2. PARTIALLY_VERIFIED evidence may support a conclusion, but uncertainty must remain explicit.\n\n3. NOT_VERIFIED means the claim must NOT be presented as established fact.\n\n4. CONTRADICTED evidence must override the original claim.\n\n5. Distinguish:\n   - confirmed fact\n   - reasonable inference\n   - unresolved uncertainty\n\n6. Do not invent missing evidence.\n\n7. Do not silently resolve disagreements between agents. If a material disagreement remains unresolved, state it.\n\n8. Do not simply summarize the previous agents. Make an independent final judgment based on the evidence hierarchy above.\n\n9. Risk severity must reflect BOTH:\n   - probability/credibility of the risk\n   - potential business impact\n\n10. If an important claim cannot be independently verified, reduce confidence rather than automatically increasing risk.\n\nPopulate the connected Structured Output Parser exactly. Do not create any additional fields or wrapper objects.\n\nDetermine:\n\nOVERALL RISK:\nLOW | MODERATE | HIGH | CRITICAL\n\nCONFIDENCE:\nLOW | MEDIUM | HIGH\n\nFINAL EXECUTIVE ASSESSMENT:\nA concise synthesis explaining the company's position and the most material implications.\n\nCONFIRMED FINDINGS:\nOnly findings sufficiently supported by the evidence.\n\nUNRESOLVED FINDINGS:\nMaterial claims that remain uncertain or insufficiently verified.\n\nCONTRADICTED / DOWNGRADED CLAIMS:\nClaims from the original analysis or critic that verification weakened or contradicted.\n\nKEY RISKS:\nThe 3-5 risks that matter most to an executive decision-maker.\n\nRECOMMENDED ACTIONS:\nConcrete follow-up actions, prioritised by importance.\n\nHUMAN REVIEW REQUIRED:\nYES | NO\n\nHUMAN REVIEW REASON:\nExplain exactly what requires human judgment or additional evidence. If none, state NONE.\nCRITICAL OUTPUT FORMAT INSTRUCTION:\n\nReturn ONLY the fields required by the connected Structured Output Parser.\n\nThe top-level object must begin directly with:\noverall_risk\nconfidence\nfinal_executive_assessment\n\nDo NOT wrap the response inside:\n- \"output\"\n- \"state\"\n- \"response\"\n- \"result\"\n- \"data\"\n\nDo NOT return markdown.\nDo NOT use ```json code fences.\nDo NOT add explanatory text before or after the structured response.\n\nThe object itself is the response.",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 3.1,
      "position": [
        2800,
        16
      ],
      "id": "public-final-adjudicator",
      "name": "Final Adjudicator"
    },
